nts><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ICHIBANGASE HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KABASHIMA TAKATOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAYAMA TADAYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI NAOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA KIWAMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAZAKI TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIZUOCHI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSAKI YOJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UEMURA ARITOMO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO SHU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ICHIBANGASE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABASHIMA, TAKATOMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAYAMA, TADAYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, NAOKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA, KIWAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAZAKI, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUOCHI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSAKI, YOJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UEMURA, ARITOMO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, SHU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical signal quality monitor for simply monitoring the quality of an optical signal with high efficiency and accuracy without inviting increase in manufacturing cost, circuit scale, and power consumption. The bit rate of a monitoring signal light beam is lower than that of a main signal light beam transmitted in an optical communication system. The reception electric bandwidth of a receiver for receiving the monitoring signal light beam is equal to or wider than that of a receiver for receiving the main signal light beam. The monitoring signal light beam includes an SOH (Section Over Head) frame. Any error in the BIP (Bit Interleaved Parity) bytes of the SOH is detected. Thus, the quality of an optical communication system, especially a light-wave network is monitored.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un dispositif de surveillance de la qualité d'un signal optique de manière simple et efficace et sans produire d'augmentation des coûts de fabrication, ni de l'échelle des circuits, ni de la consommation de puissance. Le débit binaire du faisceau lumineux du signal de surveillance est inférieur à celui du faisceau lumineux du signal principal émis par un système optique de télécommunications. La largeur de bande électrique du signal reçu par le récepteur recevant le faisceau lumineux du signal de surveillance est égale ou supérieure à celle du récepteur recevant le faisceau lumineux du signal principal. Le faisceau lumineux du signal de surveillance consiste en trames SOH (surdébit de section). On peut donc surveiller la qualité d'un système optique de télécommunications et en particulier celle d'un réseau utilisant des ondes lumineuses.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>